    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.bracketed\n\n### Description\n\nShell prompt jumps are extremely frequent for and having a configurable way to jump between them would be very nice.\r\nI do also miss them very much in zellij.\r\n\r\nI dont understand the use cases of `[P [p, ]p, ]P` as they are doing the same for me as `p` and `P`:\r\n```\r\n[\"x]]p\t\t    or\t\t\t\t\t*]p* *]<MiddleMouse>*\r\n[\"x]]<MiddleMouse>\tLike \"p\", but adjust the indent to the current line.\r\n\t\t\tUsing the mouse only works when 'mouse' contains 'n'\r\n\t\t\tor 'a'.\r\n\r\n[\"x][P\t\t    or\t\t\t\t\t*[P*\r\n[\"x]]P\t\t    or\t\t\t\t\t*]P*\r\n[\"x][p\t\t    or\t\t\t\t\t*[p* *[<MiddleMouse>*\r\n[\"x][<MiddleMouse>\tLike \"P\", but adjust the indent to the current line.\r\n\t\t\tUsing the mouse only works when 'mouse' contains 'n'\r\n\t\t\tor 'a'.\r\n```\r\nMaybe they are merely broken?\r\n\r\nAlternatively, it would be nice to have a simple wiki for common and countable jump things.",
