            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> If yes, then it is most certainly won't be a part of 'mini.bracketed' because it varies too much, i.e. doesn't really have more or less universally fixed rule to define \"start of shell output\".\r\n\r\nYes. Ok, thanks for the information. I'll close this and add some example configuration once implemented to this thread.\r\n\r\n> 'mini.bracketed' has general [advance()](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/f158f1905286e023d5848ab0b335a1cf5b8c692a/doc/mini-bracketed.txt#L605) which is used in all targets. As an example for such behavior, take a look at [conflict() target](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/f158f1905286e023d5848ab0b335a1cf5b8c692a/lua/mini/bracketed.lua#L362).\r\n\r\nAh, lol. Ok, thanks for the info.",
